    "q-60307": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60307",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "To prepare a homemade nasal spray, the ratio of salt (in grams) to cups of water is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ If Eliza wants to make a nasal spray with $15$ grams of salt, how many cups of water should she use?",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of salt (in grams) to cups of water is $\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the amount of salt and the denominator represents the number of cups of water.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $15$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 3}{2\\times 3}=\\frac{15}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $15$ grams of salt, Eliza must use $6$ cups of water.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
