    "q-147042": {
      "dom_id": "step-q147042",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The ratio of T-shirts to pairs of jeans in David's closet is $\\frac{5}{2}.$ If David has $4$ pairs of jeans in his closet, how many T-shirts does David have?",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of T-shirts to pairs of jeans in David's closet is $\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of T-shirts and the denominator represents the number of pairs of jeans.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 2}{2\\times 2}=\\frac{10}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, David has $10$ T-shirts in his closet.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
